Description: Fix GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf (CVE-2026-23864) - DoS via unbounded Server Function
 request body reaching React Server Components deserialization. The Edge-runtime
 non-multipart branch of handleAction() accumulated the entire untrusted request
 body into a string with no size cap before handing it to the vendored
 react-server-dom-* decodeReply() deserializer, which can be driven into an
 infinite loop / excessive CPU / OOM by a crafted request. Mirror the existing
 serverActions.bodySizeLimit guard already enforced on the Node non-multipart
 path so oversized bodies are rejected with 413 before deserialization.
 .
 The published npm package ships compiled JavaScript under dist/ (both the
 CommonJS build dist/server/app-render/action-handler.js and the ESM build
 dist/esm/server/app-render/action-handler.js); this patch applies the guard to
 both compiled outputs.
